---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ShotFrame from '../components/ShotFrame.astro';
import { PRODUCT } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
	title="How it works"
	description="How KSC Tower Network connects KSP pilots, browser controllers, spectators, and a hosted tower backend."
>
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="shell">
			<h1>How it works</h1>
			<p>
				{PRODUCT} is an ATC layer for Kerbal Space Program. Pilots stay in their own game
				instance. Controllers and spectators work from a web desk. A backend + LiveKit keeps
				voice, telemetry, and text in sync.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>What it is not</h2>
				<p>
					It is not a shared-universe multiplayer physics host. Each pilot flies a normal KSP
					save. Other traffic shows up as ghost vessels and radio — not as shared craft.
					Tower sees what the plugin publishes (vessel state, radio, optional camera frames)
					and talks back over voice and ACARS.
				</p>

				<h2>Rooms &amp; radio</h2>
				<p>
					The lobby lists <strong>server-owned radio channels</strong>, not free-form private
					rooms. Pilots join by tuning the in-game COM radio. Controllers join the tower queue
					(“take next call”) or open a desk on an active channel. Signed-in listeners can
					spectate a room or hear tower audio from the lobby.
				</p>
				<p>Stock public channels include:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>KSC Tower</strong> — 122.000 MHz</li>
					<li><strong>KSC Ground</strong> — 121.700 MHz</li>
					<li><strong>Global Emergency</strong> — 121.500 MHz</li>
					<li><strong>ATIS</strong> — 128.250 MHz (readout + loop; not a closeable lobby room)</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					A session scopes chat, telemetry, hull-cam, strips, checklist, squawk, callsign, and
					countdown. Voice rides a LiveKit ops room bound to that session. Release packs bake
					the API host into the player ZIP so pilots do not hand-edit URLs.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="shot-block">
				<div class="shot-grid">
					<ShotFrame
						id="lobby-channels"
						caption="Lobby — server radio channels and the controller queue."
						alt="KSC Tower Network lobby with radio channels"
					/>
					<ShotFrame
						id="radio-hud"
						caption="In-game COM — claim a channel by tuning the frequency."
						alt="In-game COM radio tuned to tower"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Pilot path</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>Install Module Manager and the KSC Tower Network GameData pack.</li>
					<li>Launch KSP — the bundled voice bridge starts with the game (Windows x64).</li>
					<li>Pair the plugin from the web app (exchange code), then tune TWR / GND / EMRG.</li>
					<li>
						Hold PTT (default <code>R</code>, or IVA RPM/MAS). Leave the beacon on to stream
						telemetry; flip it off to pause the strip without dropping voice.
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Optional mods deepen immersion without being hard requirements: ClickThroughBlocker
					for UI clicks, RasterPropMonitor / MAS for IVA PTT, kOS for ACARS scripts and a
					mirrored terminal, HullCam + JRTI for camera snapshots, Kerbalism for radiation on
					the strip. Chatterer is not recommended — live ATC overlaps badly with simulated
					chatter.
				</p>

				<h2>Controller path</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>Open the hosted tower web app in any modern browser — no KSP install.</li>
					<li>Sign in, open the lobby, and queue for the next pilot call (or assume a vacant seat).</li>
					<li>
						Work the desk: map (Kerbin, plus RSS / JNSQ / OPM plates when the pilot’s world
						matches), clearances, voice, ACARS, countdown, staging spots, and a customizable
						tower wall.
					</li>
					<li>
						Automation helps with approach sequence, separation, runway occupancy, and RP
						violations — still role-play, not physics enforcement.
					</li>
				</ol>
			</div>

			<div class="shot-block">
				<div class="shot-grid">
					<ShotFrame
						id="tower-desk"
						caption="Tower desk — map, clearances, and live strips."
						alt="Controller tower desk"
					/>
					<ShotFrame
						id="tower-wall"
						caption="Tower wall — hull-cam, countdown, radar, and more."
						alt="Customizable tower monitor wall"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Spectator path</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>Sign in with a real account (guests cannot spectate).</li>
					<li>From the lobby, hit Spectate on an active room — listen-only tower desk.</li>
					<li>Watch map, telemetry, hull-cam, and countdown; hear ops voice without PTT.</li>
					<li>
						Use the <strong>booth</strong> side channel to chatter with other spectators —
						the pilot does not hear it; the assigned controller bridges both sides.
					</li>
				</ol>
			</div>

			<div class="shot-block">
				<div class="shot-grid">
					<ShotFrame
						id="spectator-booth"
						caption="Booth — spectator commentary the pilot never hears."
						alt="Spectator booth side channel"
					/>
					<ShotFrame
						id="dragon-radar"
						caption="Dragon Radar — room-scoped hunt across the body."
						alt="Dragon Radar mini-game map"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Operator path</h2>
				<p>
					Someone has to run the network. Production needs three public pieces:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Backend API</strong> — Node service with MariaDB/Redis and auth.</li>
					<li><strong>Web SPA</strong> — the tower desk (static host or same origin as the API).</li>
					<li><strong>LiveKit</strong> — realtime voice rooms (LiveKit Cloud works fine).</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Operators set signup mode (open, invite-only, or closed), bake hostnames into the
					player ZIP, and follow the mod docs (<code>HOSTING.md</code> /
					<code>DEPLOYMENT.md</code>).
				</p>

				<h2>Roles</h2>
				<p>
					Account access climbs
					<code>guest → pilot → controller → mod → supermod → owner</code>.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Guest</strong> — lobby text chat only. No voice, plugin, DMs, or spectate.</li>
					<li><strong>Pilot</strong> — plugin, voice publish, telemetry, ACARS, Dragon Radar play.</li>
					<li><strong>Controller</strong> — tower desk, queue/assume seat, clearances, countdown, booth mute.</li>
					<li><strong>Mod+</strong> — enforcement (mute, ban, kick, close others’ rooms). Owner is pinned and cannot be banned out.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Inside a room you are also a session seat — <code>pilot</code>, <code>controller</code>,
					or <code>spectator</code>. Those are separate from your account rank.
				</p>

				<h2>Extras that ship</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Ghost fleet</strong> — render-only proxies of other pilots in your world
						(toggle on the radio). Same-world only; not shared physics.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Dragon Radar</strong> — room-scoped mini-game: find seven balls on the
						body, claim while landed, fight via ghosts + ACARS; collect all for a one-shot
						crew-restore wish. Spectators get a wall map + roster.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Clearances &amp; scorecard</strong> — takeoff / landing / taxi / hold short /
						go-around (RP only), plus auto scoring from telemetry and manual ATC notes.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Launch countdown</strong> — synced clock to the in-game HUD; start, scrub,
						cleared for takeoff.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Stream as Tower</strong> — a flight client with a stationary HullCam craft
						can publish a tower-view feed (not the Space Centre camera).
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Kerbalizer</strong> — optional send-path DSP so your mic sounds like radio
						traffic.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-started">Get started</a>
				<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/">Back home</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
